From 16fbcfaa9872775582a33d5a0778bbaceac4ad6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:20:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban chat links: classify ledger sessions once per
 origin profile, not once per row

_ledger_links called is_machine_session for every eligible origin-ledger row, so
scoped_sources (profile discovery and a state.db read per home) ran once per row
although most rows share one profile. Group the eligible refs by exact
origin_profile and call the existing bulk machine_sessions once per profile, as
_local_links does; membership is tested as str(session), the classifier's key.
Filters, row order, duplicate-uid last write, the single now and the link dicts
are unchanged; no new cache.

Tests: K bulk calls and zero per-row calls for N rows over K profiles, exact
output equality with the frozen per-row implementation over mixed rows,
changed rows/profiles observed by the next call, and the unchanged-board gate
still skipping. Synthetic 10-board bench: 127 -> 10 CPU-ms, equal outputs.
---
 hermes_cli/kanban_chat_links.py               |  22 +-
 .../test_kanban_ledger_links_bulk.py          | 242 ++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 259 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_ledger_links_bulk.py

